' Where the effective filter comes from (RFC 0009, "URL and persistence").
@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #1e1e1e
skinparam ArrowColor #1e1e1e

start
if (URL carries f or a legacy svcFilter?) then (yes)
  #fff3bf:Clauses from f=…
  (a legacy svcFilter is read as the service
  hide clause in remove mode, a stale one hides
  nothing, and the URL is rewritten as f=…);
else (no)
  :View default
  (Timeline: none. GenAI view of a GenAI trace:
  hide Non-GenAI, lift children, unless that
  would leave no span with the services hidden)
  plus the saved service default
  (localStorage, written only by Save as Default),
  unless it would leave no span;
endif
:Tree mode from tree=remove, else lift;
:uiFind text, from the URL in either case;
:Effective clauses
→ findIDs, hiddenIDs;
note right
  Every edit writes the clauses as f=…, an empty
  list as an explicitly empty f=, so that neither
  default returns on the next render.
end note
stop
@enduml
